course: dictionary
lesson: 7763
title: Purpose and on purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word purpose has a few meanings. The purpose of something is the reason it exists or the job it is meant to do. In science you might ask, «What is the purpose of the roots?» The roots take in water and hold the plant in the ground.
explain: Your purpose is what you are trying to achieve, like a goal you are working towards. In a writing lesson, the purpose of a text is why it was written, such as to inform, persuade or entertain.
explain: «On purpose» means you mean to do it; it is not an accident. «Some glasses have marks etched in the bottom to make a stream of bubbles on purpose.» The marks are made deliberately, so the bubbles are not a lucky mistake.
fact: Purpose means the reason something exists or the job it is meant to do.
fact: The purpose of a text is why it was written: to inform, persuade or entertain.
fact: «On purpose» means you mean to do it; it is not an accident.
fact: «Snubbed» means ignored or left out on purpose.
fact: When people say «It wasn't on purpose», they are explaining that a mistake was an accident.
exercise: What is the purpose of roots in a plant? | To make the plant look pretty | To keep the plant warm all winter | *To take in water and hold the plant | To make the leaves fall off
exercise: «Popeye is a cartoon that exaggerates on purpose.» What does on purpose mean here? | *It is done deliberately, meant to happen | It is done very quickly | By accident, when nobody noticed | It is done without any reason
exercise: Ayo breaks a cup and says, «It wasn't on purpose.» What is he saying? | He wanted a new cup | He broke it to show the purpose of cups | *He did not mean to break it; it was an accident | He broke it as a joke
test: In a writing lesson, what is the purpose of a text? | The colour of the page | The name of the writer | The number of words in it | *Why it was written: to inform, persuade or entertain
test: Which word means the same as «on purpose»? | Accidentally | Carelessly | *Deliberately, meaning to | By luck
exam: Which sentence uses purpose to mean what someone is trying to achieve? | *Her purpose in life is to help animals | The purpose of the dog is to bark | The chair is made of wood | The cat sat on the mat
